class Counter {

    static int count = 0;
    int id;

    static {
        System.out.println("Static block");
    }

    {
        count++;
        id = count;
        System.out.println("Instance block: " + id);
    }
    
    Counter() {
        System.out.println("Constructor: " + id);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Counter c1 = new Counter();
        Counter c2 = new Counter();

        System.out.println(Counter.count);
    }
1.How many times does the static block execute?
Only once, when the class is loaded.
2. How many times does the instance initialization block execute?
Two times because two objects are created.
3. In what order do the initialization block and constructor execute?
First, the instance initialization block executes, then the constructor executes for each object.
4. What is the final value of count?
Answer: 2
Because count++ executes once for each object.
}
